#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:4
msgid "Customize the full_deploy deployer: handling editable packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:6
msgid ""
"The built-in :ref:`full_deploy<reference_extensions_deployer_full_deploy>` "
"deployer copies the ``package_folder`` of every dependency to the deployer "
"output folder. This is what it does with the different kinds of dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:9
msgid "Packages in the Conan cache: the package contents are copied."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:10
msgid ""
"Dependencies with ``package_folder=None``, which happens when the binary is "
"skipped because it is not necessary: they are not deployed, as there is no "
"folder to copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:12
msgid ""
"Packages in :ref:`editable mode<editable_packages>`: the ``package_folder`` "
"is the local project root folder, where the ``conanfile.py`` of the editable "
"is. There is no actual \"package\" there, but ``full_deploy`` copies the "
"whole folder, including sources, build artifacts and anything else in it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:16
msgid ""
"Deploying editables is not recommended in general. Deployers are intended to "
"be customized. For real production needs, it is recommended to use your own "
"deployer, and install it with ``conan config install`` or ``conan config "
"install-pkg``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:20
msgid ""
"This is the implementation of the built-in ``full_deploy``, slightly "
"simplified, with some extra code to handle editables. Copy it to a "
"``my_full_deploy.py`` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:23
msgid "**my_full_deploy.py**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:23
msgid ""
"import os\n"
"import shutil\n"
"\n"
"from conan.errors import ConanException\n"
"from conan.tools.files import rmdir\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"def deploy(graph, output_folder, **kwargs):\n"
"    conanfile = graph.root.conanfile\n"
"    conanfile.output.info(f\"Custom full deployer to {output_folder}\")\n"
"    symlinks = conanfile.conf.get(\"tools.deployer:symlinks\", "
"check_type=bool, default=True)\n"
"    for dep in conanfile.dependencies.values():\n"
"        # Skipped binaries, there is nothing to deploy\n"
"        if dep.package_folder is None:\n"
"            continue\n"
"        # Editable packages: the package_folder is the local project folder, "
"not a package.\n"
"        # Raise a ConanException instead of \"continue\" to fail when there "
"are editables\n"
"        if dep.recipe == \"Editable\":\n"
"            conanfile.output.warning(f\"Skipping deploy of editable package "
"{dep}\")\n"
"            continue\n"
"\n"
"        folder_name = os.path.join(\"full_deploy\", dep.context, dep.ref."
"name, str(dep.ref.version))\n"
"        build_type = dep.info.settings.get_safe(\"build_type\")\n"
"        arch = dep.info.settings.get_safe(\"arch\")\n"
"        if build_type:\n"
"            folder_name = os.path.join(folder_name, build_type)\n"
"        if arch:\n"
"            folder_name = os.path.join(folder_name, arch)\n"
"\n"
"        new_folder = os.path.join(output_folder, folder_name)\n"
"        rmdir(conanfile, new_folder)\n"
"        try:\n"
"            shutil.copytree(dep.package_folder, new_folder, "
"symlinks=symlinks)\n"
"        except Exception as e:\n"
"            raise ConanException(f\"full_deploy: The copy of '{dep}' files "
"failed: {e}.\\n\"\n"
"                                 f\"You can use 'tools.deployer:symlinks' "
"conf to disable symlinks\")\n"
"        # Generators running after the deployer will point to the deployed "
"folder\n"
"        dep.set_deploy_folder(new_folder)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:65
msgid "Then it can be used as any other deployer:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:67
msgid "$ conan install . --deployer=my_full_deploy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:71
msgid "Some notes about the code:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:73
msgid ""
"``dep.package_folder`` can be ``None`` for skipped binaries, so any deployer "
"needs to check it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:74
msgid ""
"``dep.recipe == \"Editable\"`` is a valid way to detect editable packages. "
"It can also be used to implement other behaviors, like deploying only the "
"artifacts defined in the ``cpp_info`` of the editable package (``dep."
"cpp_info.includedirs``, ``dep.cpp_info.libdirs``, etc.) instead of the whole "
"folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/deployers/custom/custom_deployer_full_deploy_editables.rst:77
msgid ""
"Generators like ``CMakeDeps`` do not need conditionals for editables: the "
"``layout()`` method makes ``cpp_info`` work transparently for packages in "
"the cache and editable packages."
msgstr ""
